{
  "text": "```verilog\nmodule areset_deassert_sync #(\n    parameter CHAINS = 2,\n    parameter RST_POL = 1'b1\n)(\n    input  clk,\n    input  async_rst_i,\n    output sync_rst_o\n);\n\n    // Normalize reset polarity: internal active-high reset\n    wire rst_active = (RST_POL == 1'b1) ? async_rst_i : ~async_rst_i;\n\n    // Synchronizer chain for deassertion (release)\n    reg [CHAINS-1:0] sync_chain;\n\n    // Initialize chain to reset state (active)\n    integer i;\n    initial begin\n        for (i = 0; i < CHAINS; i = i + 1)\n            sync_chain[i] = 1'b1;\n    end\n\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge rst_active) begin\n        if (rst_active) begin\n            sync_chain <= {CHAINS{1'b1}};\n        end else begin\n            sync_chain[0] <= 1'b0;\n            for (i = 1; i < CHAINS; i = i + 1)\n                sync_chain[i] <= sync_chain[i-1];\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Output: active if either the async reset is asserted OR the sync chain is not fully released\n    // When rst_active is high, output is active immediately.\n    // When rst_active is low, output follows the last stage of the sync chain.\n    // The sync chain starts all 1s (active) and shifts in 0s.\n    // Output is active if rst_active OR sync_chain[CHAINS-1] is 1.\n    assign sync_rst_o = rst_active | sync_chain[CHAINS-1];\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
